@*
    Row-actions kebab for a results table: the design system's `.ra` (see
    `.design/handoff/ComponentsPanel.dc.html` — its `.data-table__actions` cell
    is exactly this, `btn btn--icon btn--sm` plus a `.menu`). It opens onto
    "View source", an optional "Compare with..." (which asks the host to open
    its shared release-picker modal), and "Download source".

    It was a split button with a visible "View source" segment until the design
    review. Two things were wrong with that: the handoff reserves the split
    button for a toolbar (`Publish` + caret) and puts a kebab in table rows, and
    a 32px `.btn` inside a 40px row left 4px above and below, so it crowded the
    header and the neighbouring rows. Nothing was lost by folding it in — the
    row's Name cell is already a link to the same source file, so the segment
    was a second copy of the row's primary action.

    Open / close, one-open-at-a-time, and close-on-outside-click / scroll /
    Escape are handled globally by wwwroot/row-actions-menu.js so every row
    shares one set of document listeners rather than wiring interop per row.

    PR 15b (#529) moved this off a native <details> onto the system's
    `.ra.is-open`, which is a behaviour change as well as a class swap: the menu
    no longer opens without JavaScript. The <details> was only ever half a
    fallback - the script already owned close-on-outside-click, Escape and
    one-at-a-time, so with JS off the menu opened and could only be closed by
    clicking the caret again - and the two classes collided on `.ra__menu`,
    which meant the popup we mean and the popup the design system means were
    fighting over the same rules app-wide.

    The toggle is found by `data-ra-toggle`, an attribute rather than a class,
    so a future restyle cannot silently unbind it (see #562).

    Lives in Components/Shared/ per the CLAUDE.md folder map.
*@

<span class="ra">
    <button type="button" class="btn btn--icon btn--sm" data-ra-toggle
            title="More actions" aria-label="More actions"
            aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false">
        <Icon Name="ellipsis-vertical" Width="15" Height="15" />
    </button>

    <div class="ra__menu menu" role="menu">
        <a class="menu__item" href="@ViewHref" role="menuitem">
            <Icon Name="eye" Width="15" Height="15" Css="menu__icon" />
            <span>View source</span>
        </a>

        @if (OnCompareRequested.HasDelegate)
        {
            @* Opens a shared, searchable release picker (one page-level
               modal) rather than listing every release inline per row - the
               old submenu rendered hundreds of releases on every results row
               and hung the page on a large catalogue. *@
            <button type="button" class="menu__item" role="menuitem"
                    @onclick="() => OnCompareRequested.InvokeAsync()">
                <Icon Name="git-compare" Width="15" Height="15" Css="menu__icon" />
                <span>Compare with...</span>
            </button>
        }

        <div class="menu__sep"></div>

        <a class="menu__item" href="@DownloadHref" role="menuitem">
            <Icon Name="download" Width="15" Height="15" Css="menu__icon" />
            <span>Download source</span>
        </a>
    </div>
</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>Where the primary "View reference" link points (the source viewer).</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string ViewHref { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>Download URL for the row's source file.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string DownloadHref { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// Raised when the user picks "Compare with..." - the host opens its shared
    /// release-picker modal. The menu entry only shows when a handler is wired
    /// (a callsite that doesn't support compare simply omits it).
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnCompareRequested { get; set; }
}
